        "text": "Free monthly reset credit, no activation fee since July 2025, explicit automation permission, simpler funded-phase rules on Pro, no metals halt (in early 2026)."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does MFFU have a Discord community?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes - active Discord with thousands of traders. Link from myfundedfutures.com."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What does \"sim-funded\" actually mean and is it real money?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Sim-funded = orders fill against simulated quotes (not real exchange). MFFU pays real cash from simulated profits. The distinction is fill mechanism, not payout legitimacy. Most major US futures props operate this way."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I automatically pause trading around news events for my MFFU account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "PickMyTrade includes a Trading Time feature available across all supported broker connections. You can configure specific active trading windows with start and end times (24-hour ET format). Any TradingView alerts received outside your configured hours are automatically rejected — no new trades are placed. Existing open positions remain active. Settings can be applied to specific accounts or all accounts at once. Full guide: https://docs.pickmytrade.io/docs/trading-time-settings/ For Tradovate connections, PickMyTrade also integrates with ForexFactory to automatically pause trading before and after scheduled news events — it can close open positions and cancel pending limit/stop orders during news windows. Tradovate Trading Time guide: https://docs.pickmytrade.trade/docs/trading-time-settings/"
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Does MyFundedFutures (MFFU) allow automated trading or bots?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, with limits, according to MFFU's written policy. Its Fair Play page says traders may use automated strategies tailored to their own settings as long as the tools do not aim to exploit favorable simulated fills, and high-frequency trading is not allowed on any plan. Live accounts trading with automation must follow CME guidelines. The same page bans exploiting the lack of slippage with tight brackets. The phrase about your own settings leaves off-the-shelf bots less clear, and Discord moderators have said bots are not allowed, so get a written answer from MFFU support before running a purchased bot."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I copy trade between my own MyFundedFutures accounts?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. MFFU's help center says it allows copy trading across all account types, including Tradovate's built-in group copier and external copy trading tools, and it names a preferred copier partner. You carry the risk: MFFU disclaims liability and will not provide support or resets for copy-trading problems. Copying is for your own accounts only. The Fair Play page says traders may not copy trade one another or share a device, and MFFU's Terms ban using multiple accounts to hedge, mirror or copy trades in a way that gives an unfair advantage."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is it hedging at MyFundedFutures if I go long NQ and short MNQ, or long MES and short MNQ?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Long NQ against short MNQ is hedging; MES against MNQ is not clearly covered. MFFU prohibits hedging of any kind, defined as buy and sell positions on the same underlying asset at the same time, with E-Mini and Micro NQ given as the example. Its hedging page also says hedging through different unrelated assets is permitted, though relying mainly on hedges makes your trading hard to evaluate. MFFU does not say whether correlated index pairs such as MES and MNQ count as unrelated, so ask support in writing before running that spread."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the MyFundedFutures consistency rule, and does breaking it fail my account?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on the plan, and breaking it does not fail you. MFFU's evaluation consistency rule is 30% on Rapid EOD plans and 50% on Rapid Intraday and Pro plans: no single day's profit may exceed that share of your total evaluation profit. Builder plans have no consistency rule in the evaluation but apply 50% in the sim funded stage, and the Pro 1Day add-on has none. Going over does not breach the account; you trade more days until you are consistent. Rapid sim funded payouts have no consistency rule."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I trade CPI, FOMC or NFP at MyFundedFutures?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on the account. MFFU lists FOMC meetings and minutes, the Employment Report and CPI as Tier 1 news for all traders. On Rapid Sim Funded and Pro Sim Funded accounts, trading Tier 1 news is prohibited: you must be flat with no orders from 2 minutes before to 2 minutes after, for example closed by 8:28:00 for an 8:30 release. All evaluations and Builder plans may trade Tier 1 news. On every account, straddles, strangles and other strategies that exploit the immediate news burst are banned."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "When can I take a payout on a MyFundedFutures Rapid account, and what is the buffer?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "On MFFU Rapid plans, Intraday or EOD, payouts are daily once you clear a buffer: $2,100 on 50K, $3,100 on 100K and $4,600 on 150K. The first payout is eligible 24 hours after your first trade if the buffer is met, the minimum withdrawal is $500, there is no consistency rule, and the split is 90/10. On Rapid EOD 50K, each later payout unlocks once net profit since your last payout reaches $500. Builder plans work differently, with a 50% consistency rule and caps of $1,000 or $2,000 per request, and Pro plans pay every 14 calendar days."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is the MyFundedFutures drawdown trailing intraday or end-of-day, and is there a daily loss limit?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "It depends on the plan. Rapid EOD accounts trail only on end-of-day closes: MFFU says the max loss does not move intraday and never moves down. Standard Rapid sim funded accounts trail intraday from your equity high, including unrealized profit. In both cases open losses count, and the trailing stops once the max loss reaches $100 above zero. Rapid and Rapid EOD have no daily loss limit. MFFU's payout overview says no plan has one, but its Builder 50K guide lists a $1,000 soft pause daily loss limit, so check your plan page."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can I mix minis and micros to go over my contract limit at MyFundedFutures?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "No. MFFU's Cross Instrument Policy says orders combining different instruments, such as 2 minis and 20 micros, may technically execute even when they exceed your limit, but this is not permitted, and deliberate attempts to get around position scaling are treated as a breach. MFFU's own example: a Rapid 50K sim funded account starting at 2 contracts means 2 minis or 20 micros. Three minis on one instrument is rejected; 2 minis plus 20 micros executes but can breach the account. Limits differ by plan, for example 3 minis or 30 micros on Rapid EOD 50K."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "When does MyFundedFutures move me to a Live account, and can I say no?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "You cannot decline: MFFU's FAQ says rejecting the move to a Live Funded Account is not possible. On Rapid plans, $10,000 net profit in one trading day triggers an automatic move, or the Risk Team can approve you on payout performance. Builder plans move after 5 consecutive payouts or reaching the $100K sim cap, and Pro plans are reviewed after 3 consecutive payouts or $20,000 profit. Your sim funded accounts are merged into one Live account, and Live costs such as CME professional data, commissions and platform fees come out of the Live balance."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How many funded accounts can I hold at MyFundedFutures?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "MFFU allows up to 10 active evaluations, but sim funded accounts are capped. With only 25K and 50K accounts you can hold up to 5 sim funded accounts, within plan limits: Rapid EOD 25K and 50K allow 3 each, Builder 25K allows 2, and Builder 50K allows 1. If you hold any 100K or 150K sim funded account, the cap is 3 in total across all sizes and plans. So passing two Builder 50K evaluations still leaves room for only one Builder 50K sim funded account."
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>
